X: 1
T: Bosco Stomp
O: Traditional Cajun, Louisiana
N: A Cajun two-step, recorded by Lawrence Walker and later by the Balfa
N: Brothers. Bosco is a small settlement near Lafayette.
N: From the Fiddler's Companion (Andrew Kuntz), as played by Suzie Rothfield.
N: Transposed down a major third from A, so it runs C4 to A5.
N: The last note of the third part is written A2 here; the source's A made
N: that bar an eighth short of paying back the pickup. Chords derived from
N: the melody.
